{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1304412-scion-2nd-mass-combat-system","id":1304412,"title":"Scion 2nd Mass Combat System","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-12T01:37:55-07:00","id":1304412,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Scion 2nd Mass Combat System","content":"I was trying to make a system for battles/wars too great for our usual combat system. I took inspiration in the rules from Exalted 3rd and L5R basically, but got stuck in some things (discussed by the text). They are far from essential by now, but I suppose at Demigod/God levels, they can be handy. Or, maybe at least Scions of War can find funny... Needless to say, nothing here is written in stone, and I really would like some help around.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Battle Groups</b></i><br /> Battle Groups are the main components when two groups/armies face each other. Even the most savage, brutish and uncult warlord, wanting or not, divides its forces in these groups. It's entirelly possible (sometimes, even wise) to have an army composed by different types of Battle Groups (frontliners, cavalry, aerial support, artillery, etc.).<br /> Each Battle Group is composed by the following Attributes. Treat each one as a &quot;medium&quot; for the Battle Group:<br /> <i><u>Size</u>: </i>How many members there are in this unit. (1-5)<br /> <i><u>Might</u>:</i> The offensive technological/magical power. (0-2)<br /> <i><u>Endurance</u>:</i> The general resistance (simillar to Defense, from the normal combat rules)<br /> <u><i>Tags:</i></u> Special Qualities for the Battle Group. Maybe its role in the combat, or even Special Power for it.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Size</i></u> are the main Attribute of Battle Groups, and obviously are oriented by the quantity of how many people we have in each group. The Size level represents how many dice they roll for an attack in a Mass Combat Turn.<ul><li>1 = One single combatant (not using the word &quot;person&quot; here. Giant reasons) <i>&lt;Maybe more usefull with Scale&gt;</i></li> <li>2 = around 10 people</li> <li>3 = around 100 people</li> <li>4 = around 300 people</li> <li>5 = around 1,000 people.</li> </ul>It's possible to have a Size 0 Battle Group, meaning probably the group has been defeated. It's reccomended to have groups with more than 1,000 people being divided in more Battle Groups.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Might</i></u> is a short term for many other variables. The sheer offensive power is a way to understand it, but it also means the training level and equipment of this Battle Group.<ul><li>0 = Barely trained, poorly equiped</li> <li>1 = Regular forces, regular equipment (+1e to Attack Mass Combat Rolls)</li> <li>2 = Elite forces, elite/legendary equipment (+2e to Attack Mass Combat Rolls)</li> </ul><br /> <u><i>Endurance </i></u>acts as Defense would work for a normal character. It's normally 1, or 2 if the Battle Group has any effective amor/shield to defend against what they are facing at the present moment. Ancient armors and shields may not be usually effective against present day firearms. Or maybe the other army is composed by supernal creatures that may ignore bulletproof vests.<br /> Damage suffered by one Battle Group reduces the target Battle Group's Size. When its Size reachs 0, it can not act anymore, but a retreat order may take it before that, when it get obvious that its Size is too small to keep being relevant.<br /> <br /> <b><i>The Mass Combat Turn</i></b><br /> At the start of a Mass Combat, both sides must first declare their forces. Not necessarily in a map, but both sides must be aware of how many and how different Battle Groups they are facing. Reinforcements may arrive, in according to the narrative, but at the moment, that's what each side has. At this moment, the players can assing their characters to a Battle Group at their will, leading them in where they fight better. One of the players from each army (or the SG, if this is simply the group fighting bad guys) is selected as a Commander. If a Commander had the opportunity to make previous plans for this battle (meaning, they are not under a surprise attack), they can make a roll for Strategy (that depends on how he/she is gonna make this plan. If he/she will study maps and reports of the terrain for hours, that would be Survival + [Mental]. If he's trying to remember famous battles won there, Culture + [Mental]. If he's trying to conceive some master ruse, Subterfuge + [Mental]). Any successes obtained are kept at the Strategy Pool of each army. If the Commander agrees, a Leader of a Battle Group can spend a success from the Strategy pool to get an Enhancement in any roll his/her Battle Group needs.<br /> <br /> The Battle Groups of Both sides then make Orders in turns. To decide wich side acts first, the Commanders of both sides each make a Leadership + Intellect roll, with the most successfull acting first. The first Commander then chooses a Battle Group to act first, and then enemy Commander and so on. Each Success in this roll is kept in the Order Pool for that army. Battle Groups can, at their Commander turn, move or attack by themselves as an action in their Mass Combat Turn. Anything that is not move or attack, requires an Order to be spent. Regroup, use any Power of a Leader or special soldier from any Battle Group is an Order.<br /> <br /> The Mass Combat ends when one of the armies has not any Battle Groups able to fight, or when one side declares surrender. Acceptance of surrender depends of the enemy Commander, though.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Orders to Battle Groups:</b></i><ul><li><u><i>Regroup:</i></u> The Leader of this Battle Group makes a Persuasion + [Social] roll. If any sucesses, the Size of the Battle Group recovers 1. (Troops coming from others Battle Groups already defeated, soldiers deciding not to flee, healing, etc.)</li> <li><u><i>Use a Power: </i></u>Boons, Knacks or Relics special powers. Legendary Creatures/Denizen Special Abilities.</li> <li><u><i>&quot;Stand Your Ground!&quot;:</i></u> The Battle Group receives +1 Endurance while mantain its position.</li> <li><i><u>Anything Special: </u></i>Demoralize the enemy, inspire your troops, challenge an enemy Leader to a duel... Feel free to get creative.</li> </ul><br /> If by any reason the Battle Group of the Commander is took out of the combat (defeated, retreat, Commander knocked uncounscious, etc.), his army can not make use of Strategy and Order pools.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Tags for Battle Groups:</b></i><ul><li><i>Ranged: </i>If there are no enemy Battle Groups engaged with this Battle Group, they can attack an enemy Battle Group.</li> <li><i>Armored</i>: Treat this Battle Group as having Armor (Heavy). (It has a &quot;Size Damage box&quot; that can doesn't affect its real Size)</li> <li><i>Brutal</i>: The successes necessary for a Critical Stunt are reduced by 1.</li> <li><i>Special Mobility</i>: The Battle Group may move not normal distances as a move action. Ex.: Cavalry, aerial support, subterranean movement troops, etc.</li> <li><i>Toxic</i>: And enemy Battle Group damaged by this Battle Group suffers the Poisoned Condition (similar to the one from normal combat rules). For a number of Mass Combat Turns equal to the margin of succes for this attack, the Battle Group suffers -1 Size.</li> </ul><br /> Other Tags/Flairs are welcome, but the core books already offer many that can be used here, as Incorporeality, In/Vulnerability, Inspiration, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T11:00:23-07:00","id":1304468,"title":"","content":"My idea when conceiving this system was to make general and diverse rules as possible. Appliable to WWI soldiers firing from trenches, Spartan troops &quot;fighting at shade&quot;, huge dragons raining fire from the skies, aerial bombards, archers firing from tall towers to troops under them, samurai armies colliding in melee charges, or even scenes where one single Legendary Elite Badass soldier hacks tens of enemies with a single blow (Dinasty Warriors says that it's possible)... All of that.<br /> <br /> They are still pretty simple. Even with the idea already in my mind at some time, I just wrote these rules directly to the forum at 5 AM, and as such, we have not so many options about Orders or Tags. I would really appreciate some help with these.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Order pool is a good idea at this point. It works fine when it works (all the sides have many Successes in that pool to spend later), but my worries are when one Commander simply hasn't any and then... &quot;We walk and we attack, guys. That is it&quot;. Maybe having a minimal of Orders depending of the number of different Battle Groups he has at his command would be a good idea... Kind of thing that needs testing imo.<br /> <br /> Maybe the &quot;Use a Power&quot; needs specifying that for that power to be effective in a Mass Combat. Feats of Scale sound like a good idea. But Powers like Bolt from the Blue seems perfectly usable in large scale by themselves, so... Also needs testing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23841,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","user":"Hayashi","date":". 04-12-2019, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T12:05:45-07:00","id":1304481,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s really nice way of setting the values to an specific standard. I didn\u2019t get to any part of Scion for large scale combat, but in TC Core there is on page 118-120 if I am not wrong. There is a post on TC forums with a very related content, it\u2019s wrongly named B, but take a look.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like the idea of mass combat with variable values according to the adversary as it\u2019s set on TC, I can understand it\u2019s not the focus of the game, but there could be a value to it, and it should be possible for a single character (or Vehicle) to face an army (we are talking Aberrants and Gods, came on...)<br /> <br /> I would start by the Antagonist description, Mook for starting troops, to Villain to highly trained, giving Monster only to superhuman troops (heroes and denizens). Than I would use your ideas to adjust the characteristics of an army (unity, what ever it\u2019s named). Than Size would add its value to the Soft Armor, add scale enhancements to the rolls (when apply) and things like that, but would add complications to mobility. Might and Endurance could enter as Attack and Defence Enhancements, working as equipment extras or in combination with the tags. Didn\u2019t give a very deep thinking about it, but looks like it would work.<br /> <br /> I would use your ideas of Orders and Tags, they are really interesting. We could create different unities just by changing the tags, not worrying about the size, training or anything. Orders could be special actions the army trained under the command of an specific character and its available only when they work together.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s my initial impression and feedback... I think it could work when the characters are powerful enough to face armies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T14:24:10-07:00","id":1304507,"title":"","content":"This is a great post I was just working on porting over Exalted Battle Groups (EX3) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1304069-b\">here</a>. And I stumble on your post with some very nicely crafted options.<br /> <br /> I would make the Command Roll like a Teamwork roll with stunts. The orders above could be stunts with success costs.<br /> <br /> Anyway have to run right now I need to reread this and ponder on it. I think Mine was a very basic bare bones approach thinking I would use EX3 with Storypath core mechanic on top of it.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T16:38:59-07:00","id":1304530,"title":"","content":"One of the joys or ease of the EX3 mechanic was you could bolt on Battle Group stats to any character turning it into a battle group.<br /> <br /> So my desire would be to use standard Storypath NPC statistics / mechanics and have a system (Battle Groups) that bolts onto both the NPC and Storypath Core Mechanic.<br /> <br /> So my design objectives would be to change as little as possible and as much as nesessary. <br /> <br /> For me a Battle Group should be a grouping of Scale and options for the commanders. I Should be able to take the Centaur they just previewed and attach a Battle Group to it.<br /> <br /> I like a lot you have prepared. I would not drop Drill and mash it with Might, I think it has a place. I like your add of endurance very useful. <br /> <br /> The item I am trying wrap my mind around is using the Storypath health example centaur and tacking on for the battle group. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T09:10:36-07:00","id":1304633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1304412-scion-2nd-mass-combat-system?p=1304530#post1304530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the joys or ease of the EX3 mechanic was you could bolt on Battle Group stats to any character turning it into a battle group.<br /> <br /> So my desire would be to use standard Storypath NPC statistics / mechanics and have a system (Battle Groups) that bolts onto both the NPC and Storypath Core Mechanic.<br /> <br /> So my design objectives would be to change as little as possible and as much as nesessary.<br /> <br /> For me a Battle Group should be a grouping of Scale and options for the commanders. I Should be able to take the Centaur they just previewed and attach a Battle Group to it.<br /> <br /> I like a lot you have prepared. I would not drop Drill and mash it with Might, I think it has a place. I like your add of endurance very useful.<br /> <br /> The item I am trying wrap my mind around is using the Storypath health example centaur and tacking on for the battle group.<br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was re-thinking all that. I really would like the system to allow the &quot;Battle Group of a single man&quot;. Not just for &quot;Dinasty Warrior-like warriors&quot;, but because technically, a single and enormous dragon, warmachine, giant, warship, avatar of a God, etc. would be, by definition, a Size 1 Battle Group. Simply say that &quot;That depends&quot; would let the Size system open to an undesirable relativity. Maybe to forsake the idea of &quot;Size&quot; and ponder that (or simply the attack) by another variable more relevant to this would make more sense...<br /> <br /> This is basically my big problem with the Size 1 Battle Group. It has only one die to attack and vanishes after one damage (ok, we can say that to inflict this one damage is pretty hard, considering Endurance/Armor/whatever), but that doesn't sound in accord to the epic that &quot;kill a giant dragon&quot; should have. Maybe remodel Endurance as more like a Health system can do that.<br /> <br /> So... Instead we make Attack in accord to Size, how would be if we create another Attribute in the Battle Group in for Attacks? (Let's call it - in a surge of creativity - by 'Attack'). It's the same as the Attack Roll for the single character (Size 1 Battle Group), or, in case we have an army of Centaurs, their medium value of Attack Rolls. I think it works because: &quot;We need to make a Battle Group made of [insert Denizen here]. What is their Attack value? Their Attack Roll. And that is it&quot;. Maybe a larger group can apply Scale too, when attacking a lesser group...<br /> <br /> PS.: I was playing Shogun Total War 2 yesterday, and didn't realize how this system is similar to their system of &quot;units&quot;. I think it's good. I love that game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T15:56:57-07:00","id":1304711,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s possible to think of the battle group as a higher scale creature, being higher in Size, Power and Resistance, maybe with a lower mobility or something.<br /> <br /> You than add some tags for special effects and properties of the battle group and allow the Commander to \u201ctake control\u201d of the battle group by Orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T16:20:29-07:00","id":1304712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1304412-scion-2nd-mass-combat-system?p=1304711#post1304711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s possible to think of the battle group as a higher scale creature, being higher in Size, Power and Resistance, maybe with a lower mobility or something.<br /> <br /> You than add some tags for special effects and properties of the battle group and allow the Commander to \u201ctake control\u201d of the battle group by Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, adding the Battle Tag Group:...<ul><li><i><b>Large (1-4): </b></i>The Battle Group is still composed by a single creature, but behaves instead as a creature of size comparable to a larger scale for Attacks and suffering damage.</li> </ul><br /> I was about to write an equivalence table for &quot;How many people this measure of power should suffice&quot; (Since it makes, in short words, make a Group Size 1 be so agressive and resistant as a Size 5)... And then got stuck in the problem itself. A solution would be to think as &quot;how many people this unit/warrior/thing can knock out in a single blow?&quot; and then use that as its &quot;new Size&quot; by that Tag. But then... I think it would simpler just to say &quot;This thing has a Size (nearly or not) of a single human being but is able to cleave tens of normal soldiers per attack&quot; (Sauron in LotR movies for reference). So... Not necessarilly adding the Tag, just changing the thinking about Size. Numbering the people in the Battle Group is ok, but I think this case of a &quot;Single Elite Badass Unit&quot; (SEBU for short) it more an exception/special case of the rule.<br /> <br /> I thought too about adding a Tag to allow the BG attack many targets spliting its dice pool. But... I don't think a Tag is necessary for that. It's then from now and forward implicit that any Battle Group should be allowed to split Attack Rolls.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:19:04-07:00","id":1304720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1304412-scion-2nd-mass-combat-system?p=1304633#post1304633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't the Battle Groups dice pool be based on their stats? <br /> <br /> So for example<br /> <br /> ANTAGONISTS: CENTAURS [SCION: ORIGIN]<br /> Scion<br /> <br /> Archetype: Professional<br /> Qualities: Group Tactics, Natural Weapons (Hooves), Twitchy<br /> Flairs: Here I Come<br /> Drive: Eat, drink, and be merry!<br /> Primary Pool (7): Agility, Archery (+1 Enhancement), Creative Pursuits<br /> Secondary Pool (5): Kicking, Endurance, Survival<br /> Desperation Pool: 3<br /> Health: 2<br /> Defense: 2<br /> Initiative: 7 <br /> <br /> So these stats would be modified the Battle Group. <br /> <br /> The size of a creature and the size of a battle group will be two different things. So a Battlegroup of Ogres may be a size 1 Battle Group with 10 ogres and ogres may be large creature with a Storypath Scale 1 for size. <br /> <br /> Not sure if that makes sense. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:26:58-07:00","id":1304723,"title":"","content":"So just using the Centaurs and comparing a fight of 1 centaur vs 10 centaurs.<br /> <br /> Solo Centaur 5d Kick vs <br /> 10 Centaurs (Sz1 BG) Defense 2<br /> <br /> 10 Centaurs 5d Kick +2 BG Scale vs <br /> Solo Centaur Defense 2<br /> <br /> The Centaur BG could have an addition Health box or as Hard Armor to give it longer sticking power to win the fight and in the long run it should win. <br /> <br /> Putting them over to top would be a commander giving orders with possible bonuses based on his successes, strategy, etc. <br /> <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 04-13-2019, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T19:51:37-07:00","id":1304749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1304412-scion-2nd-mass-combat-system?p=1304720#post1304720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why wouldn't the Battle Groups dice pool be based on their stats? <br /> <br /> So for example<br /> <br /> ANTAGONISTS: CENTAURS [SCION: ORIGIN]<br /> Scion<br /> <br /> Archetype: Professional<br /> Qualities: Group Tactics, Natural Weapons (Hooves), Twitchy<br /> Flairs: Here I Come<br /> Drive: Eat, drink, and be merry!<br /> Primary Pool (7): Agility, Archery (+1 Enhancement), Creative Pursuits<br /> Secondary Pool (5): Kicking, Endurance, Survival<br /> Desperation Pool: 3<br /> Health: 2<br /> Defense: 2<br /> Initiative: 7 <br /> <br /> So these stats would be modified the Battle Group. <br /> <br /> The size of a creature and the size of a battle group will be two different things. So a Battlegroup of Ogres may be a size 1 Battle Group with 10 ogres and ogres may be large creature with a Storypath Scale 1 for size. <br /> <br /> Not sure if that makes sense. <br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exactly what I meant. One battle group would have a tag of \u201cScale\u201d that would affect all the attaches, defences and any thing the number of individuals would help, also can add some complications when the number is a problem. Additionally, you can add weapon and armor tags to the battle group to define their equipment.<br /> <br /> So a single fighter, if can\u2019t rise the scale, will not be able to hurt a battle group scale 3, and it would sum up with the size of the creature, so a Scale 2 battle group of giants size 1 is a scale 3 for porpoise of combat.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say a Scale 5 is composed of 1000 individuals, a god of war could rise his scale to fight all of them on the same scale. As with size scale, a shockwave tag can be added to the attack, as the group can fire to several targets at same time, as well as any other tag that may fit.<br /> <br /> In game terms, the battle group is a single antagonist, basically an individual of higher scale, but on narrative it would be a bunch of soldiers. Each soldier is not better than any other, but they work fine as a group, and the injuries an individual can do to the battle group with a few hundred soldiers would not matter much to the group, needing another group of similar size (or a Hero with the proper capacity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}